.Dt PQAC 7
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pqac
.Nd post-quantum access control: exoteric mediation, esoteric observation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
is a short paper.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mandoc -T pdf pqac.7 > pqac.pdf
mandoc -T lint pqac.7
.Ed
.Sh ABSTRACT
Post-quantum
.Em cryptography
is a claim about the residual hardness of named problems
.Pq lattices, hashes, codes
when the adversary's uniform class is
.Em BQP
rather than
.Em BPP .
Post-quantum
.Em access control ,
as used here, is a different claim: that the defender's
.Em authorization
relation is not an instance of such a problem, and therefore does not
collapse under Shor or Grover.
.Pp
The defender is a classical stored-program machine
.Pq von Neumann: one linear store, code as data, binary words
running a
.Fx
kernel with
.Xr mac 4
hooks.
The adversary is quantum: polynomial-time quantum algorithms on the
usual public-key names, Grover search over unstructured domains, and,
as a working hypothesis, coupling to the electrical and electromagnetic
plant
.Pq power distribution network, return, near-field
including entanglement or entanglement-enhanced metrology.
The adversary is
.Em not
assumed to be executing a quantum ISA on the defender.
.Pp
.Em Exoterically ,
discretionary access control, lattice mandatory access control, and
MMU translation are interpreted predicates over credentials, labels,
and address-space metadata.
They do not reduce to discrete logarithm or period-finding.
A BQP adversary who would
.Em act as
a subject must still produce a classical write accepted by the vnode
path, the MAC policy module, and the translation lookaside.
What remains BQP-sensitive is
.Em authentication
.Pq binding a name to a subject before a label attaches :
.Xr sshd 8 ,
TLS, package signatures, then
.Xr login.conf 5 .
.Pp
.Em Esoterically ,
those predicates are themselves electrical events.
A page-table walk is current on a rail; a label in a system extended
attribute is a pattern of stored charge that, when interpreted, switches
bitlines.
The in-band/out-of-band cut is an alphabet cut
.Pq syscalls versus analog traces ,
not a cut in the physics.
If an observation function on the plant has a kernel-visible subject
in its factorization, the monitor still constrains the support of the
observation.
If it does not factor, the monitor is silent.
Independence of the observation from high objects is
.Em imperviousness
.Pq a non-interference statement .
A quantitative bound on leakage is
.Em resistance .
These are not interchangeable.
Quantum advantage on the plant is not a corollary of Shor.
Packaging
.Em A_M
on GENERIC
.Pq rc.d, Xr setfsmac 8 , ZFS, login classes, a 2001 PLM
supplied operational lemmas the slogans omit: empty lattices,
first-match combinators, obsolete
.Em Obj
alphabets, the login cut, RDTUN ifnets, and recovery as part of
the monitor.
.Sh MACHINE AND ADVERSARY
.Ss Defender
A von Neumann host: shared store, sequential fetch, binary encoding.
.Fx
GENERIC provides
.Ql options MAC .
We take
.Xr mac_lomac 4
as the integrity policy
.Pq floating labels, low-watermark
and Unix DAC as the residual access matrix on the same objects.
The MMU implements a function from
.Pq virtual page, privilege, rights
to
.Pq frame, fault .
Virtual memory may revoke
.Xr mmap 2
mappings when LOMAC demotes a subject
.Pq Xr mac_lomac 4 ,
.Va security.mac.mmap_revocation .
The TCB is the kernel plus the loaded policy modules.
.Xr mac 9
does not claim complete root containment; neither do we.
.Pp
This is not a quantum architecture.
Qubit memory, CPTP evolution as the instruction semantics, and
no-cloning as a confinement axiom are out of model.
CHERI-style capabilities would be a different classical machine;
they are not this paper.
.Ss Adversary
Uniform class
.Em BQP
plus Grover's quadratic over unstructured search
.Pq oracle
.Em O : {0,1}^n -> {0,1} ,
expected
.Em O(2^{n/2})
queries.
Shor's algorithm places integer factorization and discrete log in
.Em BQP ;
the usual PKI names
.Pq RSA, finite-field DH, ECDH, ECDSA
are therefore not authentication against this adversary.
Grover does
.Em not
yield a symbolic executor, a confused-deputy oracle, or a kernel-bug
finder.
Unstructured search over a 32-bit ASLR slide is incomparable to
finding a
.Xr mac 9
hook bypass.
.Pp
Plant coupling
.Pq T3
is hypothesized, not demonstrated here: a completely-positive
instrument on some electromagnetic degree of freedom correlated with
defender computation, possibly entanglement-enhanced
.Pq spin squeezing, NV-center or SQUID magnetometry
beyond the standard quantum limit toward the Heisenberg limit.
A 300 K CMOS die and copper PDN are a thermal bath; decoherence
times for macroscopic entanglement with the rail are not assumed
generous.
T3 asserts only that some distinguishing observation may exist, not
that it is cheap.
.Ss Out of scope
Replacing the naming path with ML-KEM, ML-DSA, or SLH-DSA is
necessary and insufficient.
Necessary: otherwise the adversary forges the name that
.Xr login 1
will label.
Insufficient: a correctly named subject is still mediated by DAC, MAC,
and the MMU, which never consulted the modulus.
.Sh EXOTERIC: NAMING AND MEDIATION
Authentication binds an identity to a process.
Authorization relates that process to objects and to regions of the
store.
The first, on contemporary
.Fx ,
is cryptographic or a local console.
The second is an access matrix
.Pq DAC: owner-directed
.Xr chmod 2
and
.Xr chown 2 ,
uid/gid
composed with a lattice policy
.Pq MAC
composed with translation rights
.Pq MMU .
.Pp
Let
.Em Sub
be subjects
.Pq credentials
and
.Em Obj
objects
.Pq vnodes, mappings, sockets, ifnets .
DAC is a function
.Em A_D : Sub x Obj -> 2^{ops}
modifiable by the object's owner.
MAC is a function
.Em A_M
computed from labels
.Em lambda(s) , lambda(o)
in a partial order
.Em (L, preceq)
and not owner-modifiable.
Anderson's reference monitor
.Pq complete mediation, isolation, verifiability
is approximated by
.Xr mac 4
entry points on vnode, VM, IPC, and network objects.
Complete mediation is an aspiration;
.Xr mac 9
states that not all attack channels on a privileged subject are
hooked.
.Pp
Shor destroys
.Em A_auth
when
.Em A_auth
is RSA/ECC.
It does not inhabit
.Em A_D
or
.Em A_M .
There is no reduction from period-finding to
.Ql lomac/high
or to the allocation of a PTE.
A BQP adversary who would become
.Em s
in
.Em Sub
must still induce a classical state the hooks accept.
That is
.Sy quantum-adversary-stable mediation :
the decision procedure's complexity class is not the source of its
security, because the decision is not a cryptographic game.
It is an interpreted predicate in the kernel.
.Sh LATTICES
Bell-LaPadula is a secrecy lattice: no read up, no write down.
Biba is an integrity lattice: no read down, no write up.
.Xr mac_lomac 4
is Biba-like integrity with
.Em subject relabeling
on read-down: a subject at grade
.Em g
that reads an object at
.Em g' < g
is demoted toward
.Em g'
.Pq low-watermark, floating label .
Subsequent writes to objects dominated by the old
.Em g
fail.
Auxiliary grades
.Ql [aux]
and ranges
.Ql (lo-hi)
exist for exec-time assumption and for administrative exemption
.Ql equal .
.Pp
This axiom is
.Em not
non-interference for secrecy.
Goguen-Meseguer non-interference, and the observational-determinism
and unwinding lemmas used to prove it, speak to whether high inputs
are visible in low outputs.
LOMAC
.Em permits
the read that secrecy forbids, then removes write-up.
A side-channel thesis about emanations of high
.Em secrets
is therefore not discharged by LOMAC; it would want MLS, Biba's
no-read-down, or an enclave whose observation function is specified
in analog.
LOMAC's short proof, and the reason this suite uses it, is
integrity:
a sandbox subject cannot write-up into high OS objects after a low
read.
.Pp
.Xr setfsmac 8
composes specfiles by
.Em first match
.Pq later regexes for the same path are dropped silently .
That is a policy combinator, not a lattice operation; overlays must
precede the official PLM or a leading
.Ql /dev
catchall
.Ql equal
rule shadows later high device nodes.
.Sh MECHANISM DIVERSITY
DAC, MAC, and MMU are not replicas of one lock
.Pq replication would share one specification and one failure .
They are three interpretations of
.Dq may this subject disturb this region
with distinct failure modes:
.Bl -bullet
.It
DAC fails when an owner
.Pq or a hijacked uid
grants
.Em ops
the lattice would refuse.
.It
MAC fails when an object is unlabeled, when
.Ql equal
is over-applied, when first-match drops a high rule, or when a hook
is missing
.Pq Xr mac 9 .
.It
MMU fails when a mapping is granted that the lattice would later wish
revoked, when a wild pointer is already in-kernel, or when
microarchitectural leakage
.Pq Spectre-class
reads across translations the PTE still forbids architecturally.
.El
.Pp
A quantum adversary who factors one modulus walks around all three.
A quantum adversary who obtains a classical write still faces the
other two if the write is not already supervisor-mode.
Diversity is not a work factor in
.Em n
and does not grow with qubits.
It is the absence of a single specification whose one bug is total.
.Pp
Login remains the cut.
.Xr login.conf 5
attaches
.Em lambda(s)
after authentication.
A forged name is a forged subject.
Isolation after a correctly named login is what
.Xr mac_lomac_grok 8
and
.Xr mac_grok 8
implement: groups as roles, official contexts, ZFS recursive
snapshots as recovery, PREINSTALL as behavioral restore.
That practice is not argued here; the manuals argue it.
.Sh ESOTERIC: THE OBSERVATION FUNCTION
Extend the system with an observation alphabet disjoint from syscalls.
Let
.Em Tr
be executions
.Pq traces of hooks, translations, and pipeline switching
and let
.Em O : Tr -> H
map a trace into a Hilbert space
.Pq or, classically, into a time series in R^k :
supply current, chassis potential, near-field
.Em B ,
impedance echo on the adapter primary.
TEMPEST, SPA/DPA, and RAMBO-style bus modulation are the classical
.Em O .
T3 asserts that some quantum instrument may refine
.Em O .
.Pp
.Em In-band
is the syscall alphabet.
.Em Out-of-band
is
.Em O .
Both are functions of the same electrons.
A PTE walk is not adjacent to the PDN; it
.Em is
a PDN event.
A
.Xr chmod 2
is charge in a line.
The clerk's cut
.Pq kernel story versus physics
does not imply that authorization is
.Dq not electrical .
It implies that the kernel names only some of the electrical events.
.Pp
Say
.Em O
.Em factors through a subject
when there exists a projection
.Em pi : Tr -> Sub
.Pq the kernel-visible principal whose switching dominated the analog
and a map
.Em O' : Sub x Tr -> H
with
.Em O = O' o (pi x id)
in the relevant coordinates.
Then constraining
.Em pi Ns 's
image
.Pq who may run, which objects they may map, whether they are demoted
constrains the support of
.Em O .
Sandbox credentials, LOMAC demotion, seeotheruids, and page rights
become statements about which traces are in the domain of a useful
.Em O' .
That is resistance, if one then bounds
.Em I(high; O)
or an analogous distinguishing advantage.
.Pp
Say
.Em O
.Em does not factor
when an authorized hot core, or the idle plant, already yields a
distinguishing observation of high objects with no unprivileged
modulator.
Then
.Em A_D ,
.Em A_M ,
and the MMU are silent:
the computation is allowed, and
.Em O
reads it.
The remaining claims are physical: constant-power dual-rail logic,
filtered PDN, Faraday, spatial isolation of high work.
Those do not follow from
.Pa mac_lomac.ko .
.Pp
.Em Imperviousness
is observational equivalence: for all traces
.Em t, t'
agreeing on low inputs,
.Em O(t)
and
.Em O(t')
are indistinguishable
.Pq trace distance, or a computational distinguisher with the adversary's instrument .
That is non-interference with respect to
.Em O ,
not with respect to
.Xr write 2 .
POSIX MAC does not supply it.
LOMAC in particular supplies the wrong axiom for emanation
.Em secrecy :
the authorized trusted subject computing on a high object
.Em is
the hot core
.Em O
wanted.
.Ss Cost of T3
Shor is a clean reduction in the quantum circuit model against a
named algebraic problem.
Coupling
.Em O
to a multilayer board at several gigahertz, under a ground plane,
in GENERIC's background switching, is an experimental physics
problem.
Entanglement with the rail must survive a thermal bath, or the
enhancement must be in the
.Em sensor
.Pq squeezed spin, NV, SQUID
not in a Bell pair with the victim's electrons.
Placement, bandwidth, a correlator, and usually a local modulator
remain.
The modulator, if required, is a process, hence a candidate for
.Em pi .
Do not take quantum advantage on the plant as a lemma from BQP.
.Sh THESES
Deniable separately.
.Bl -tag -width T3xx
.It T1
Membership in
.Em BQP
does not by itself produce a classical write accepted by the
reference monitor.
.It T2
.Em A_D ,
.Em A_M ,
and MMU translation are quantum-adversary-stable mediation on a von
Neumann defender.
They are post-quantum access control in that sense, and not
post-quantum cryptography.
.It T3
.Pq working hypothesis
Some instrument on the plant, possibly entanglement-enhanced,
can distinguish defender computation.
.It T4
If
.Em O
factors through a kernel-visible subject, T1 and T2 constrain
.Em O .
If not, T1 and T2 are silent and the property is physical
non-interference.
.It T5
Quantum advantage for
.Em O
is not free.
Decoherence, placement, and distinguishing a vnode in GENERIC's
noise are the adversary's burden, not Shor's corollary.
.El
.Pp
T1 and T2 are implemented by this suite's rc.d packages.
T3 is assumed so that T4 is utterable.
T4 is two theorems until a coupling map is exhibited.
T5 keeps T3 from swallowing T1 and T2.
The following lemmas are residue from building those packages and
from Handbook and mailing-list failures that the slogans do not
mention.
